A||N||16||xfilesgirl1||NEED INFO ON 84 & 85 FIERO!||||10||
Z||000000||xfilesgirl1||09-29-2000||01:48 AM||||I'm looking to buy my first car and I was wondering what the pros and cons are of a 1984 and 1985 fiero. thanks,<BR>Alisa||||reg||10
Z||000001||DaRkLoRD||09-29-2000||05:08 AM||||Hi Alisa, welcome to the forum!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Are you looking to buy a 4cyl or a V6?<P>in 1984 all the Fieros had 4cyl engines, but in 1985 the V6 model was introduced in the SE and GT.. and of course the 4cyl was still available in both the SE and Coupe models.<P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||10
Z||000002||theogre||09-29-2000||06:04 AM||||Unless you find an 84 in really good shape or otherwise special to you then go with 85 or later.<P>84 has some unique quirks that can be real annoying. It has diferant wiring in allot of places and other subtle things a first year car has.<P>from 85 on things are more uniform across models and years.<P>88's have similar draw back as 84's. Pontiac made huge changes to the car's suspension and brakes. because there are so few of them it can be hard to get parts for 88's. Allot of things from earlier years don't fit 88.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||StuGood||09-29-2000||06:51 AM||||...and don't forget that the 1987-88's have bigger gas tanks and more reliable headlight doors  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> !<P>If you've determined that it's going to be a 1984-85, I'd go with the 1985 model everytime unless I wanted the 1984 pace car model). ||||reg||1
Z||000004||BroCar 87||09-29-2000||07:18 AM||||HEY Alisa, don't let these guys be too hard on you about the 84's, some of our forum members will swear by thiers. Although, there was a bad batch of rods that came out in the 84 models.<BR>I AM going to have to go with the 85 though. There is more interchangeability with other models. Do you know if it is a GT or SE or Coupe??<BR>Either way, I DO hope you get a FIERO!!! You will love it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>Also, what area do you live in? What part of the country??  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif"><P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/NorthFLFieroSIG.jpg">    <BR>87 Coupe "IRON BEAST"<BR>84 SE (project)||||reg||12
Z||000005||HugGRRRFiero||09-29-2000||10:59 AM||||Welcome to the forum Alisa!<P>Between an '84 or '85, I'd go with an '85.<P>Mine's a '84 SE  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR><P>------------------<BR>          <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/huggrrr.gif">        <BR>        <A HREF="mailto:HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com">HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com</A> ||||reg||7
Z||000006||Rodrv6||09-29-2000||04:06 PM||||First, welcome to the forum!  As the owner of an 84 since it was new, here's my .02 worth.  If you don't want a 6 cylinder and don't think you will ever want to swap to a 6 cylinder engine down the road, then either year should be fine.  You might be able to find an 84 for a little less than a comparable 85 since they are a little less popular because they only came with a 4 cylinder and are difficult to convert.  If you think you will ever want a 6, then go with an 85 or newer.  Hope you find one to enjoy!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Rod Schneider, Woodstock, Ga.  84 SE||||reg||6
Z||000007||ROB MAC||09-29-2000||05:04 PM||||The PRO - coolest go kart ever built.<BR>The CON - if you aren't prepared to learn how to do 60 to 75% of the repair, tune-up and tweaking yourself it can be an EXPENSIVE hobby for a first car. Some places around here charge $1,200.00 to replace a clutch. ||||reg||1
Z||000008||xfilesgirl1||09-29-2000||05:53 PM||||hi...thanks for your reply. I'm looking for a V6. I was thinking of going with a 85. I found one. it's an automatic. I don't know how to drive standard yet. Just learning to drive. It's $1500.00 and it doesn't have a safety. I should be looking at it soon.<BR>though.<BR>thanks,<BR>Alisa<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by DaRkLoRD:<BR><B>Hi Alisa, welcome to the forum!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Are you looking to buy a 4cyl or a V6?<P>in 1984 all the Fieros had 4cyl engines, but in 1985 the V6 model was introduced in the SE and GT.. and of course the 4cyl was still available in both the SE and Coupe models.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||1
Z||000009||xfilesgirl1||09-29-2000||05:55 PM||||Hi,<BR>thanks for relpying. I'm not sure  if I want a SE, COUPE OR GT, but I'm definitely happy with either.<BR>thanks,<BR>Alisa<P>oh...and I live in manitoba, Canada.<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by BroCar 87:<BR><B>HEY Alisa, don't let these guys be too hard on you about the 84's, some of our forum members will swear by thiers. Although, there was a bad batch of rods that came out in the 84 models.<BR>I AM going to have to go with the 85 though. There is more interchangeability with other models. Do you know if it is a GT or SE or Coupe??<BR>Either way, I DO hope you get a FIERO!!! You will love it   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>Also, what area do you live in? What part of the country??   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif"><P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||1
Z||000010||xfilesgirl1||09-29-2000||05:58 PM||||thanks for the help guys,<BR>I am in autobody, going into mechanics and welding at school. I am defintely going into autobody and mechanics in grade 11 too. I wouldn't mind majoring in it either. I love it so much. But I'm the only girl in my autobody/power mech/welding class.<BR>but it's fun.<P>thanks,<BR>ALisa<BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by ROB MAC:<BR><B>The PRO - coolest go kart ever built.<BR>The CON - if you aren't prepared to learn how to do 60 to 75% of the repair, tune-up and tweaking yourself it can be an EXPENSIVE hobby for a first car. Some places around here charge $1,200.00 to replace a clutch. </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||1
